        "Key Findings from the Visualization:\n",
        "Absence of Support is Common: The vast majority of high-risk (bad credit risk) clients have no other debtors or guarantors (mapped to 'None') and no other installment plans (mapped to 'None'). This corresponds to the highest count bar in the chart (over 180 applicants).\n",
        "Other Installment Commitments: For high-risk applicants who do not have any debtors or guarantors, a significant portion already has other installment plans with Banks (around 54 applicants), indicating they may already be financially leveraged.\n",
        "Guarantors and Co-applicants: A very small number of high-risk applicants have a co-applicant or guarantor, and almost all of those have no other installment plans."
