        "## Project Summary: German Credit Risk Analysis & Prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Project Goal\n",
        "The objective of this project was to analyze the **German Credit dataset** (from the UCI Machine Learning Repository) to identify key characteristics that distinguish **Low-Risk (Good)** credit applicants from **High-Risk (Bad)** applicants, and to build a predictive Machine Learning model to automate the assessment of creditworthiness.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Key Exploratory Insights\n",
        "Through extensive data visualization and exploratory analysis, identified several strong indicators of credit risk:\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Financial Commitments & Support:** High-risk clients rarely have external support like co-applicants or guarantors. Additionally, those who are already leveraged with other installment plans (particularly through banks) present a higher likelihood of default.\n",
        "* **Credit Duration & Amounts:** There is a direct, strong positive relationship between the credit duration (repayment term) and the requested credit amount. High-risk clients tend to request longer terms (**median of 24 months**) compared to low-risk clients (**median of 18 months**).\n",
        "* **Demographics (Sex and Personal Status):** Single males made up the largest total volume of both high and low-risk loans. However, divorced/separated/married females and single males carried the highest sheer counts of high-risk defaults within their categories.\n",
        "* **Loan Purpose:** Loans requested for **Business** or **Education** purposes had significantly higher percentages of high-risk classifications, whereas loans for **Cars (used)** and **Retraining** were historically much safer.\n",
        "* **Employment and Job Type:** Skilled employees constitute the highest volume of borrowers, but risk is distributed across all job categories, with self-employed and management personnel carrying higher individual amounts.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. Machine Learning Model Results\n",
        "Constructed and evaluated a **Random Forest Classifier** to predict creditworthiness based on all available applicant attributes:\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Model Accuracy:** **75%** of the test cases were correctly classified.\n",
        "* **Low-Risk Detection (Good Credit):** Highly effective with a **92% Recall**, making it a robust safeguard for identifying eligible borrowers.\n",
        "* **High-Risk Detection (Bad Credit):** Achieved **66% Precision** but a lower **35% Recall**, indicating that handling class imbalance (more good credit examples than bad credit) remains an area for future optimization.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Key Decision Drivers (Feature Importance)\n",
        "The Random Forest model ranked the following four characteristics as the most critical factors in determining credit default probability:\n",
        "1. **Credit Amount** (How much money is requested)\n",
        "2. **Status of Existing Checking Account** (Current financial standing/liquidity)\n",
        "3. **Age** (Stability and stage of life)\n",
        "4. **Duration of Credit** (The period over which the credit is distributed)"
      ]
